backend/scripts/ml/models/incumbent/*.pkl
backend/scripts/ml/models/incumbent/*.json
# The preserved previous model, kept so quick_eval.py can score the incumbent on
# the SAME holdout as a challenger. It is a local artifact of a retrain, not
# source: best_model.pkl is 12MB and features_holdout.pkl is 183MB. RETRAIN.md
# step 0 says how to populate it, and the gate FAILS rather than shrugging when
# it is absent, so an unpopulated directory can never quietly skip the check.

# The trained crowd model is NOT distributed with this repo. Both artifacts were
# tracked until 2026-08-18, when the repo was prepared to go public under
# PolyForm Noncommercial; they were removed from the index with `git rm --cached`
# (which is why these rules are live now and were inert before -- .gitignore never
# applies to an already-tracked path).
#
# READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING IT, because the failure is silent by design. With no
# artifact on disk, mlPredictor.loadModel() logs one line ("Model files not found
# -- using rule engine"), returns false, and every prediction for the life of the
# process is answered by crowdEngine.js and tagged predictionMethod
# 'rule_engine'. That is the honest-refusal path and it is correct behaviour, but
# it means the PRODUCTION DEPLOY MUST NOW DELIVER THESE TWO FILES TO THE RAILWAY
# CONTAINER BY SOME ROUTE OTHER THAN GIT. Nothing in the boot sequence fails if
# they are absent; the API just serves the rule engine and no alarm fires.
#
# A cloner is not expected to have them. backend/scripts/ml/models/README.md
# explains how to train their own from their own data using ../train/.
backend/scripts/ml/models/crowd_model.onnx
backend/scripts/ml/models/model_metadata.json

