# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ML training directory: DEFAULT-DENY, then re-admit source by name.
#
# Enumerating what to ignore has now failed three times, because a working file
# only has to miss the pattern by one character. `*.pkl` does not match
# `train_val_split.pkl.stale-2026-03-14` (208 MB), and `*.log` does not match
# `train_v25.log.stale`. Both were sitting untracked and unignored, one
# `git add -A` from a public repo.
#
# So the rule is inverted: everything in train/ is ignored, and the source
# files are re-admitted explicitly. A new artifact with any suffix is ignored
# by default; a new SOURCE file has to be named here, which is a one-line
# change made by the person who added it, at the moment they add it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend/scripts/ml/train/*
!backend/scripts/ml/train/*.py
!backend/scripts/ml/train/*.js
!backend/scripts/ml/train/*.sh
!backend/scripts/ml/train/requirements.txt
